+src/router/reg-exp-router/node.ts:94 — the sibling-conflict check now fires only when the new pattern is exactly `.*`, so a param pattern may silently coexist with literal siblings instead of raising UnsupportedPathError, and the resulting single-alternative regexp drops handlers (`/post/new` + `/post/:id` returns only the static handler for `/post/new`, and `/entry/:name` + `/:user/entries` returns only the first route), while the unchanged literal-branch check still throws in the reverse registration order, making acceptance order-dependent.
+src/router/reg-exp-router/node.ts:150 — the `\\${k}` escape was replaced by a bare `${k}`, so literal regexp metacharacters in a path are emitted unescaped: `/v1.0/:id` now also matches `/v1X0/abc`, and a path containing `(` or `)` produces an invalid RegExp (SyntaxError, not UnsupportedPathError, so SmartRouter cannot fall back).
+src/router/reg-exp-router/node.ts:65 — `i <= len - 1` is always true inside the `i < len` loop (the old test was `restTokens.length === 0`), so a non-terminal `*` token compiles to `.*` instead of `[^/]+` and `/a/*/b` now matches across slashes, e.g. `/a/x/y/z/b`.
